winewayland: an app's main window is never a subsurface of the window under its corner (GitHub Neutron#28)

The owned-subsurface rule falls back to win32u's owner_hint when a window has no GW_OWNER. For an
unowned window that hint is NtUserWindowFromPoint(left - 1, top - 1): whatever lies just past the
top-left corner. A modal dialog placed over the main window's corner made Photoshop 2025's main
window a wl_subsurface of its own Open dialog: drawn from the dialog's client origin and off the
screen, then gone once the dialog closed.

Use the hint only for windows the Windows taskbar would not list (WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW without
WS_EX_APPWINDOW, like the Premiere Button Editor the rule was written for), and never when the
window owns the hinted window. Reproduced and verified with harnesses/ownerhint-dialog.c on a
nested KWin: main window inside the dialog on 135 (3/3), in place on the fix (2/2), the tool-window
control still becomes a subsurface. Kill switch: NEUTRON_OWNER_HINT_STRICT=0.

--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/window.c
@@ -510,6 +510,46 @@
     return on;
 }
 
+/* NEUTRON (GitHub Neutron#28): may the owned-subsurface rule treat owner_hint as the owner of a window that has NO
+ * owner? owner_hint is not an ownership fact. For an unowned window win32u computes it as
+ * NtUserWindowFromPoint(window.left - 1, window.top - 1) -- whatever window happens to lie just past the top-left
+ * corner. For the Premiere Button Editor that is the main frame, which is what the rule was written for. For an APP'S
+ * MAIN WINDOW it is whatever covers its corner, and a modal dialog usually does: Photoshop 2025's main window became a
+ * wl_subsurface of its own Open dialog, drawn from the dialog's client origin and off the screen, and vanished when the
+ * dialog closed (harnesses/ownerhint-dialog.c reproduces both).
+ *
+ * The line Windows draws is the taskbar's: an unowned window gets its own taskbar button -- it is an independent
+ * application window -- unless it is WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW, and WS_EX_APPWINDOW forces one. Only a window the shell would NOT
+ * list (the Button Editor is WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW|NOACTIVATE|TOPMOST) may borrow the window under it as an owner. And never
+ * a window it owns itself: Windows keeps an owned window above its owner, so nesting the owner inside it inverts that.
+ * Kill switch: NEUTRON_OWNER_HINT_STRICT=0 restores the unconditional fallback. */
+static BOOL neutron_owner_hint_usable(HWND hwnd, HWND hint)
+{
+    static int on = -1;
+    static HWND last_hwnd, last_hint;
+    DWORD ex;
+    HWND o;
+    int depth;
+    const char *why = NULL;
+
+    if (!hint || hint == hwnd) return FALSE;
+    if (on < 0) on = neutron_gate("NEUTRON_OWNER_HINT_STRICT", TRUE);
+    if (!on) return TRUE;
+    ex = NtUserGetWindowLongW(hwnd, GWL_EXSTYLE);
+    if ((ex & WS_EX_APPWINDOW) || !(ex & WS_EX_TOOLWINDOW)) why = "it is an independent app window (taskbar rule)";
+    for (o = hint, depth = 0; !why && o && depth < 32; o = NtUserGetWindowRelative(o, GW_OWNER), depth++)
+        if (o == hwnd) why = "it owns that window";
+    if (!why) return TRUE;
+    if (hwnd != last_hwnd || hint != last_hint)
+    {
+        ERR("neutron-ownerhint: hwnd=%p (ex=%08x) stays a toplevel, not a subsurface of owner_hint=%p: %s\n",
+            hwnd, (unsigned)ex, hint, why);
+        last_hwnd = hwnd;
+        last_hint = hint;
+    }
+    return FALSE;
+}
+
 /**********************************************************************
  *          neutron_maxkeep_fix
  *
@@ -1152,8 +1192,9 @@
             DWORD st = NtUserGetWindowLongW( hwnd, GWL_STYLE );
 
             /* GW_OWNER is NULL for exactly the windows this is meant to catch; owner_hint is the
-             * value win32u actually passed us and it is correct. */
-            if (!gwowner) gwowner = owner_hint;
+             * value win32u actually passed us -- but for an unowned window it is only the window
+             * under the corner, see neutron_owner_hint_usable (#28). */
+            if (!gwowner && neutron_owner_hint_usable( hwnd, owner_hint )) gwowner = owner_hint;
 
             /* CAPTIONED OWNED WINDOWS ARE INCLUDED as of 2026-08-27. The previous rule excluded
              * them because a subsurface cannot be moved by the COMPOSITOR. True -- but the reason
